This one I&#39;ve asked about before and never gotten an answer to.&nbsp; Your statement was my understanding at first, but then I realized that by that reading, when Bunker is in Out Of Suit Mode, he can never get back in the suit.&nbsp; It&#39;s unclear whether he can simply climb back in as an action, or if it takes so long it can only be done in a Montage scene, or what.

[/quote]

His Out of Suit dice section says &quot;When he can use the suit again, change to Operations Mode&quot;

As a Gm, I&#39;ve taken this to mean: When Vance is out of Bunker, he has to make an effort to be allowed to get in Bunker, wherever that suit may be. If he is at a fancy dress military ball, perhaps the suit is in a trailer in the parking lot, and Vance must Overcome to get through the crowd without panicking them, reaching the trailer, thus qualifying for &quot;Can Use Suit&quot;. If he is taking a shower when the alarms at Freedom Plaza go off, Vance would Overcome to get dry and dressed enough not to injure himself or the suit, qualifying&nbsp; for &quot;Can use suit&quot;. If he is giving a commencement address at a university with the suit on stage behind him, he might only have to say &quot;Goodbye&quot; and turn around in order to qualify for &quot;Can use the suit again&quot;.

I think a more interesting question is exploring how a Vance player would voluntarily get out of the suit,&nbsp;<em>be unable to enter into that same suit</em>, and then need to shenanigan to qualify for &quot;I can haz Suit&quot; again, all in one scene. (Self-destruct/trapped, call in Freedom Plaza&#39;s supply drones for newer/older suit that he totally has, as per collected trade, Minor Twist, must wait two rounds, gets back into suit dropped off by drones.)
